  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Secondary and Tertiary Healthcare Services Project in Southern Lebanon (Tyre Public Hospital)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at improving the access to quality public healthcare services in Southern Lebanon through constructing and equipping a 70-beds public hospital in Tyre District. The project is planned to benefit more than 280,000 inhabitants and will contribute to the reduction of the number of patients seeking medical care outside the district by 50%.

The project is part of the Framework Agreement (FWA) signed between the GoL and IsDB for the Reconstruction Program for Lebanon. The project also supports thrust III of the IsDB Vision 1440H i.e. &#x201c;Promotion of health of the population of member countries&#x201d;. The Government of Lebanon (GoL) allocated its financial contribution for land acquisition, for parts of the civil/electromechanical works of the hospital and for hiring the consultancy services related to detailed engineering design, civil works supervision and medical equipment. IsDB finances all the remaining scope of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
